The file frontend/.env currently contains:

  VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

  VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:3001

Delete frontend/.env entirely. Do not replace it. The production build must

NOT set these env vars so that at runtime the browser uses

window.location.host (config.js already has this logic: it falls back to

`${defaultProto}//${defaultHost}` when not on localhost). If you delete

the .env, the dynamic detection works correctly on Render.

FIX 1C — There are hardcoded localhost strings in component source files

that bypass config.js entirely. The built JS bundle contains these:

  const ts = "http://localhost:3001"   (used in multiple fetch calls)

