run BharatBazaar as a separate process on the same web service port.

Correct approach: On Render, BharatBazaar backend/server.js must run as

part of the same Node process OR you must configure the External mode to

gracefully show a "demo not available in hosted mode" message instead of

crashing silently. Do one of:

  OPTION A: In server.js, when NODE_ENV=production and environment=EXTERNAL,

  spawn BharatBazaar as a child process internally on a non-exposed port

  (e.g. 15001) and proxy through the existing server. Update .env.example

  and render.yaml to document this.

  OPTION B (simpler): In the frontend External mode, show a banner:

  "External mode requires local BharatBazaar instance. Run npm start locally

  for the full demo." This is honest and avoids silent failures.

  OPTION B is safer for a submission where no commit is allowed after.

  Pick B: in the ExternalMode/BharatBazaar components, add a check for

  whether the API_URL is not localhost and if so, show the banner.

